class BoletoHTML:
    def __init__(self, width=750, widthCanhoto=0, fontSizeTitle=9, heightLine=27, fontSizeValue=12, title="Boleto bancário"):
        self.width = width
        self.widthCanhoto = widthCanhoto
        self.fontSizeTitle = fontSizeTitle
        self.heightLine = heightLine
        self.fontSizeValue = fontSizeValue
        self.title = title
        self.content = []

    def add_header(self, text):
        # Add header content to the boleto
        self.content.append(f'<div style="font-size: {self.fontSizeTitle}px;">{text}</div>')

    def add_body(self, key, value):
        # Add body content to the boleto
        self.content.append(f'<div style="font-size: {self.fontSizeValue}px;">{key}: {value}</div>')

    def add_footer(self, text):
        # Add footer content to the boleto
        self.content.append(f'<div style="font-size: {self.fontSizeTitle}px;">{text}</div>')

    def add_page_break(self):
        # Add a page break to the boleto
        self.content.append('<div style="page-break-after: always;"></div>')

    def save_to_file(self, filename):
        # Save the generated HTML content to a file
        with open(filename, 'w') as file:
            file.write('<html><head><title>{}</title></head><body>'.format(self.title))
            file.write('\n'.join(self.content))
            file.write('</body></html>')
```

This code defines a `BoletoHTML` class with the specified fields and methods. The class allows you to build an HTML representation of a bank slip by adding headers, body sections, footers, and page breaks. Finally, you can save the generated HTML content to a file using the `save_to_file` method.
