### Program Overview

This Python script uses a trackball sensor connected to a Raspberry Pi running Raspbian to simulate mouse movements and clicks on the computer. The trackball's movement and button presses are translated into corresponding mouse actions using the `xte` command-line tool. The script continuously reads input from the trackball and updates the mouse position accordingly.

### Classes and Structs

#### TrackBall Class

